  "data_quality_notes": [
    "Only 831/5798 nodes have a true `origin_year` (the rest fall back to `first_seen_year`); treat `year` as a 'first appeared in this corpus' proxy, not a verified invention date.",
    "TEMPORAL LEAK, FOUND AND FIXED: filtering snapshots on `year` (falls back to `origin_year`) instead of `first_seen_year` let nodes into a snapshot before the corpus had any record of them \u2014 334 nodes at cutoff=2020, 332 at 2022, 143 at 2024. Snapshots are now built on `first_seen_year` (nodes) and `provenance.article_year` (edges); see the module docstring.",
    "49/1429 hyper-edges have a `provenance.article_year` earlier than the max `first_seen_year` among their member nodes. This is expected and handled correctly: it is exactly why 'dropped_partial_edges' occurs at intermediate cutoffs even though the edge's own article_year is <= cutoff.",
    "277 distinct surface forms map to more than one node id across the whole dataset (584 node ids total), suggesting duplicate entities not merged at export time (e.g. the same technique recorded once per article, or once per type). Worst case: 'graph neural networks' spans 4 separate ids. These are NOT merged automatically; the clustering method may need a de-duplication pass, or this should be treated as a known limitation of the raw export."
